Copyright 2026 The NInfer 4090 Windows Contributors

This product includes software developed by:
- Neroued (https://github.com/Neroued/ninfer)
  Canonical upstream NInfer inference engine: C++20/CUDA core, DFlash2,
  ReplaySSM, and Paged KV Cache. Licensed under Apache License 2.0.

- UDPSendToFailed (https://github.com/UDPSendToFailed/ninfer-4090)
  Creator of the original RTX 4090 fork and pioneer of the WDDM
  evictable-budget bypass on Windows WDDM and of E8 lattice (Conway-Sloane)
  geometric quantization (rk4v4-e8). The --wddm-evictable-budget feature
  and the rk4v4-e8 KV storage in this branch originate in that fork.

- sergiuszm (https://github.com/sergiuszm/ninfer-4090)
  Ada Lovelace sm_89 kernel optimizations, rk4v4-e8 adaptation, and the
  GDN cooperative-launch fix.

- natpate (https://github.com/natpate/ninfer-windows)
  Base Win32/MSVC portability layer, unbuffered asynchronous I/O
  (OVERLAPPED), and the initial Windows scripts.

- headpiece747 (https://github.com/headpiece747/ninfer-5090-windows)
  Native Windows MSVC compilation base from which this branch descends
  (C-runtime compatibility patches, Windows dependency tooling, FFmpeg
  integration).

- Don-Chad (https://github.com/Don-Chad/ninfer-3090)
  Pioneering work on the Ampere architecture and early compatibility
  bridges; reference Windows/MSVC adaptations and build configurations.

This product contains modifications by the 4090 fork contributors to support:
- Native Windows 11 MSVC compilation on Ada Lovelace (sm_89), with kernels
  adapted to the 48 KiB static shared-memory limit
- Integration of rk4v4-e8 (real 4-bit quantization over Conway-Sloane E8
  lattices) as a KV cache storage
- Multi-Token Prediction (MTP3) and DFlash legacy speculative profiles on
  Qwen3.6-35B-A3B
- WDDM evictable-budget residency lock (--wddm-evictable-budget, v1.0.6):
  D3D12/DXGI-based negotiation with the Windows WDDM memory manager,
  enabling 260k-token rk4v4-e8 KV contexts at C=4

Model foundations (weights distributed under their own licenses):
- Qwen Team (Alibaba Cloud) - foundational model architectures (Qwen3.6/Qwen3.8 families)
- unsloth (https://huggingface.co/unsloth) - NVFP4 quantizations
- z-lab (https://huggingface.co/z-lab) - DFlash/DFlash2 companion weights

